-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/e2b6edb4-ad3d-513c-b7dc-e77c36070add
-- title:
--   Centring non-supersingular places at good points after a level automorphism
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q \ge 5$ is a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. The field $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` is equipped with a valuation subring $A$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in `A.nonunits`. Two function fields occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change (inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) of the full modular function field of level $M'$, and `fieldBar q M' = xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the $q$-expansion field of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$-modular functions, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, that is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   The remaining data fall into groups.
--
--   *Supersingular places downstairs.* A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ is given, with `hW` saying that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic curve of invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   *Reduction of the level-$M'$ field.* $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $x \mapsto x \bmod \mathfrak m_A$ on constants, with $A$ recovered as the preimage of the constants, with every nonzero element scalable into the integers with nonzero residue, together with a map `placeMap` on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of elements of nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that any Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` and has $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo $\mathfrak m_A$.
--
--   *Igusa components.* A primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` is fixed, and `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` denotes the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` chosen to satisfy `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` (the prescribed action on ratios of integral $q$-expansions, conjugated by `conjElem q γ`, under the identification sending $\zeta'$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$), the identity automorphism when no such automorphism exists. A family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$ is given, subject to: `hIg_inf`, which identifies $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at the line `lineInfty q` as the Gauss ring, $f \in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if $f\,y = x$ for some Laurent series $x, y$ with coefficients in $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction; `hIg`, which produces for each line $\ell$ some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ` and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which says that for all $\zeta'$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the preimages of the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family.
--
--   *Supersingular rings.* A family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $W$ is given, with four hypotheses: `hSS_A`, that a constant $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when $x \in A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` which is regular wherever $j$ is (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $j$-element `coeffEmb _ jq` implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that every $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own preimage under each `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   *The prolongation.* $R$ is a `RegularProlongation A (fieldBar q M') (xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M'))`, i.e. a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` with a surjective residue map onto the characteristic-$q$ level field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants and with every nonzero element scalable into the integers with nonzero residue; `hR` identifies `R.integers` with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O` says that $f$ lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   *Ramification and base-field data.* An element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ is given. A subfield $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is given, together with $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$, and the hypotheses that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, has algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. An auxiliary prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$ is given, together with $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is given with a valuation subring $A_1 \subseteq K_1$ equal to $A \cap K_1$ (hypothesis `hA₁`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for `fieldBar q M'` viewed as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $F_0$ be any $k_0$-subfield of `fieldBar q M'` subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, any finite family $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and any $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the image of $K'$ satisfying $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ has all $a_i = 0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of `coeffEmb`. Write $T_1$ for the compositum `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (image of K₁) ⊔ F₀` inside `fieldBar q M'`. Let $T_1$ carry an $A_1$-algebra structure whose structure map agrees with the inclusion of $K_1$ into `fieldBar q M'` on $A_1$, and let $j_1 \in T_1$ be a nonzero element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the $j$-function, the class of `coeffEmb _ jq` transported by `hle`.
--
--   On the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) — the pushout of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along the middle chart — four auxiliary notions are introduced for the statement. For $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$: `InStalk x f` holds when for every point $y$ of `XFin` with `ιFin.base y = x` there are $g, h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$, and likewise for every point $y$ of `XInf` above $x$ with `chartAlgInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$ in both charts. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational (the constants surject onto its residue field) and for every $f \in T_1$ with `InStalk x f` the image of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ lies in $A$, and the $A$-valuation of that value is $< 1$ precisely when `InMax x f`. Finally `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of: the image of $x$ under `toBase` is the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; every point to which $x$ specialises equals $x$ (so $x$ is closed); for every point $y$ of `XFin` above $x$, every $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `R.integers.nonunits` belongs to $y$; the same for `XInf` and `chartAlgInf`; and for every point $y$ of `XFin` above $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   The assertion is then the following. Let $P$ be a rational place of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and suppose that for every $s \in W$ the following statement fails: for all $f \in$ `R₀.integers` satisfying the $j$-regularity condition (for every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, nonnegativity of the order of the $j$-element implies nonnegativity of the order of $f$) and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in $A$ and in $\mathfrak m_A$. Then there exists $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ such that `GoodPt x` holds and `Centred (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ • P) x` holds, where the action is the transport of places by the level automorphism.
--
--   This is the covering step for the smooth Igusa base model: every rational place of the geometric full-level function field that avoids all the supersingular tubes can, after applying a level automorphism in $\Gamma_0(M')$, be centred at a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model which lies on the $\infty$-Igusa component and over an ordinary $j$-invariant. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks), where the residue discs of the model are taken to be the sets of places centred at such points.
